content.text:
The implementation boundary is now clear:

- fix the router so absolute notification targets can never be folded into the current chat route;
- add a first-class `parent_event_id` to `knowledge.save`, backed by the existing event-thread field, so a derived Behavior event is a real reply to the source post;
- add durable idempotency keys to Behavior-authored events and notifications, because reaction scripts are retried up to three times and today can duplicate side effects;
- move Social Radar’s save/deliver work into a deterministic reaction script, keep the model responsible only for ranking/explanation, and codify its entity types/Behavior in the pruned personal-agent config;
- link the digest to Memory with both source and reply event IDs, so each thread renders the original post, its external link, and the agent’s answer.

I’m writing the red tests for those contracts before touching implementation.

